WEBVTT

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:42.830
We're home.

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:52.630
What's wrong, Tohru?
You seem to want to be spoiled today.

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:55.180
Because...

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:57.140
Were you being a good boy?

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:01.020
Yeah!

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:04.350
All right, good boys get rewards.

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:41.220
Take that! Battle Proton Beam!

00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:45.480
Hyper Altema!

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:53.820
Let me join!

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:55.900
Who are you?

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:57.030
You got a weapon?

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:58.530
Weapon?

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:11.500
Tohru...

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:13.250
What's wrong?

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:18.800
Why are you here?

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:21.680
Because I'm your mother, Tohru.

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:23.060
That's not right...

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:26.390
Because, you both are...

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:31.690
What's wrong, Tohru?

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:34.190
Did you have a bad dream?

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:36.530
You were scared, right?

00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:23.010
Reuniting: A Bitter Dream

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:40.070
Big Brother.

00:04:41.530 --> 00:04:43.450
Yeah. Does it hurt?

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:48.080
I'm fine. What about Tohru?

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:51.160
Don't worry about him.
You should rest up.

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:07.890
This can't be the end, can it, Tohru?

00:05:27.450 --> 00:05:28.410
Kyoka...

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:31.290
What's wrong?

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:34.870
Kyoka, your injury isn't bothering you?

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:36.670
What injury?

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:38.960
I mean, Kyoka, you were—

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:41.920
Tohru, are you all right?

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:45.680
You're acting strange, you know?
You're drenched with sweat.

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:46.680
Well...

00:05:46.890 --> 00:05:49.680
Don't tell me.
Was it my big brother again?

00:05:50.390 --> 00:05:53.180
No, that's not it...

00:05:54.230 --> 00:05:58.480
Moments ago, over there...
my parents were standing there.

00:05:58.480 --> 00:05:59.730
Yeah, and?

00:05:59.730 --> 00:06:01.780
But they can't be alive!

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:04.030
The accident—

00:06:05.150 --> 00:06:06.860
Isn't that nice?

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:09.320
You can be together with them forever.

00:06:17.290 --> 00:06:19.880
I'm sorry, I gotta go.

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:23.420
Where are you going?

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:24.170
Where?

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:27.220
Well... I have to protect—

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:28.390
Protect who?

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:38.140
Who... is that?

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:40.560
I'm right here, you know?

00:06:41.310 --> 00:06:43.110
I have to fight.

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:46.280
If I don't, everyone will die.

00:06:46.490 --> 00:06:48.200
Even Sidune...

00:06:48.410 --> 00:06:50.570
Is something wrong with me?

00:06:55.620 --> 00:07:01.080
Didn't I already say?
You don't have to force yourself to fight.

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:03.340
You should do
what you want to do, Tohru.

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:05.710
Yeah, that's why...

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:09.680
I wanted to protect everyone.

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:11.800
But, you're scared?

00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:13.510
I am scared.

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:15.270
But...

00:07:15.270 --> 00:07:18.560
Tohru, you were sad that Sidune died,

00:07:19.350 --> 00:07:21.150
but it's okay now.

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:24.900
Everyone will be here,
forever and always.

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:28.030
That's not right...

00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:32.320
Sidune died. He shot her.

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:37.040
Hey, what does it matter
if you're alive or dead?

00:07:38.660 --> 00:07:40.080
Who are you?

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:43.590
I'm Kyoka Katagiri.
Have you forgotten about me?

00:07:43.590 --> 00:07:46.550
No, you're not Kyoka!

00:07:46.550 --> 00:07:48.420
Then, who would you prefer, Tohru?

00:07:49.090 --> 00:07:50.260
Is it me?

00:07:52.010 --> 00:07:54.010
Or is it me?

00:07:56.720 --> 00:07:57.720
Is it me?

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:02.350
So it's me after all?

00:08:37.180 --> 00:08:39.310
Tohru, where are you going?

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:42.980
He's a boy, so it's good
to see him full of energy.

00:08:43.480 --> 00:08:45.560
Tohru, where are you going?

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:48.940
No matter where you go,
it's the same thing.

00:08:48.940 --> 00:08:49.690
Tohru.

00:08:49.860 --> 00:08:50.780
Tohru.

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:51.900
Tohru.

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:13.130
Oh, here you are!

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:15.890
Where are you going in such a hurry?

00:09:17.970 --> 00:09:18.970
That way?

00:09:26.690 --> 00:09:27.520
No...

00:09:27.520 --> 00:09:28.650
Then, that way?

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:38.450
Hey, Tohru?

00:09:38.950 --> 00:09:42.540
No matter how much effort you put in, Tohru...
no matter how much you fight...

00:09:42.950 --> 00:09:45.000
You can't escape from time.

00:09:45.830 --> 00:09:49.130
Because everything has already ended.

00:09:56.840 --> 00:09:58.090
It's fine.

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:00.810
You should rest up, Tohru.

00:10:02.140 --> 00:10:06.270
That's right. Relax... and close your eyes.

00:10:08.190 --> 00:10:09.770
So warm...

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:13.610
Is this... really all right?

00:10:13.780 --> 00:10:16.110
You're fine. It's all right.

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:26.960
You were groaning.
Were you having a dream?

00:10:28.380 --> 00:10:31.040
Yeah, a scary dream...

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:34.880
It's all right. I'll be here forever.

00:11:00.950 --> 00:11:02.740
What kind of picture did you draw?

00:11:02.740 --> 00:11:03.910
Um...

00:11:11.080 --> 00:11:13.290
HELP ME

00:11:14.050 --> 00:11:16.460
That's right, I...

00:11:17.170 --> 00:11:18.050
Tohru?

00:11:38.820 --> 00:11:41.280
We finally meet...

00:11:43.410 --> 00:11:45.160
How mysterious.

00:11:45.370 --> 00:11:49.000
Is this the truth
behind the Desert Syndrome?

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:51.500
Remy...

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:53.040
Sir Tohru?

00:11:53.710 --> 00:11:54.590
Let's go back.

00:11:55.300 --> 00:11:57.710
We need to quickly
prepare our countermeasures.

00:11:58.260 --> 00:11:59.470
Understood.

00:12:06.140 --> 00:12:07.640
Are you all right?

00:12:10.600 --> 00:12:11.730
You...

00:12:12.940 --> 00:12:14.310
Where am I?

00:12:14.650 --> 00:12:17.650
You've been swallowed up
by the Dead End.

00:12:18.150 --> 00:12:19.360
Dead End?

00:12:20.570 --> 00:12:22.360
I'm referring to that sand.

00:12:22.660 --> 00:12:23.910
That's right.

00:12:24.450 --> 00:12:27.870
Remy used an Energy Cube
and turned into sand...

00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:30.960
Just what is this really?

00:12:31.250 --> 00:12:34.880
An Energy Cube causes time
to advance to the future.

00:12:35.090 --> 00:12:38.590
In other words, it accelerates time forward.

00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:41.260
Doctor Odhner also mentioned that.

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:43.180
Then why did Remy turn into sand?

00:12:44.050 --> 00:12:48.180
Because that was his future,
as it is for all of you...

00:12:49.180 --> 00:12:52.190
That sand... is our future?

00:12:57.770 --> 00:13:01.570
Let me tell you the story,
from where it all began...

00:13:09.790 --> 00:13:10.580
This is?

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:15.080
This is the end of our solar system,
the Heliopause.

00:13:16.380 --> 00:13:18.670
The basic technology behind time control

00:13:18.670 --> 00:13:23.550
was initially found in this strange particle
drifting through outer space.

00:13:25.430 --> 00:13:32.480
The Energy Cube was developed from that particle,
and it was easy to mass-produce.

00:13:33.100 --> 00:13:35.100
Easily mass-produced, huh?

00:13:35.350 --> 00:13:36.150
Right.

00:13:36.400 --> 00:13:39.520
And the time machine technology
was soon applied to something else.

00:13:39.770 --> 00:13:41.030
Something else?

00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:43.740
It was being used for military operations.

00:13:45.910 --> 00:13:51.080
Eventually, humanity would use the time machine,
and find another world in an alternate time-space.

00:13:51.240 --> 00:13:54.960
However, both worlds
had internal chaos hidden within.

00:13:54.960 --> 00:13:58.250
The two worlds meeting
would not be fortunate.

00:13:58.710 --> 00:14:02.710
A giant war encompassing both worlds started.

00:14:04.970 --> 00:14:06.340
Follow me.

00:14:12.600 --> 00:14:15.940
Tohru, what do you think
is the ultimate weapon?

00:14:16.640 --> 00:14:20.940
Ultimate? Doesn't that depend
on the situation and objective?

00:14:21.230 --> 00:14:24.650
There are times a gun is useful,
and others when you need a knife.

00:14:24.650 --> 00:14:28.530
Right. Then, let's make it
so you can use both.

00:14:30.120 --> 00:14:31.200
Anything else?

00:14:31.490 --> 00:14:32.910
Let's see...

00:14:33.240 --> 00:14:36.870
Let's give it the ability
to self-evolve and to learn.

00:14:39.290 --> 00:14:44.090
But no matter how strong the weapon,
if you drop it, it's useless.

00:14:45.090 --> 00:14:46.090
Then...

00:14:48.260 --> 00:14:51.260
Now, you'll never drop it again.
Anything else?

00:14:51.600 --> 00:14:54.930
Even if you can't drop the weapon,
if they aim for the body...

00:14:56.100 --> 00:14:56.890
Right.

00:15:10.490 --> 00:15:16.580
The perfect weapon is one with human form
and makes any and every type of attack possible.

00:15:16.960 --> 00:15:22.130
Ultimate and perfect, where time ends...
that, in fact is...

00:15:26.130 --> 00:15:29.840
That is what the sand...
Dead End... really is.

00:15:30.390 --> 00:15:35.100
By having the Energy Cube advance time,
Dead End is created.

00:15:35.430 --> 00:15:40.480
We used Dead End in our war.

00:15:41.400 --> 00:15:47.570
No, I should say that we thought we were using it,
but we were being used by Dead End.

00:15:49.240 --> 00:15:56.080
Dead End, with the power to absorb
all sorts of energy and matter, analyze it, and replicate it,

00:15:56.080 --> 00:15:57.750
is the ultimate weapon.

00:15:58.830 --> 00:16:02.670
Those that use Dead End
become part of Dead End.

00:16:03.040 --> 00:16:07.920
And those that lose against Dead End
become absorbed by Dead End.

00:16:08.260 --> 00:16:09.840
What lies beyond...

00:16:11.680 --> 00:16:15.720
...is a world where Dead End
has swallowed everything.

00:16:17.100 --> 00:16:19.600
It's what brings an end to the world.

00:16:19.980 --> 00:16:22.190
That's why it's called Dead End.

00:16:22.480 --> 00:16:25.400
Then, who are the Timekeepers?

00:16:25.650 --> 00:16:28.360
Why do they give us Energy Cubes?

00:16:28.940 --> 00:16:32.360
The countless humans swallowed up
into the Dead End

00:16:32.360 --> 00:16:35.410
have melded their psyches
and harbor one will.

00:16:36.080 --> 00:16:38.620
That is the Timekeepers.

00:16:39.910 --> 00:16:46.090
The Timekeepers, after swallowing all of humanity
from my world, headed to the past.

00:17:22.210 --> 00:17:25.500
I came here to stop that from happening.

00:17:30.420 --> 00:17:34.180
But if the world turns into sand,

00:17:34.630 --> 00:17:36.720
why did the Timekeepers come to the past?

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:38.300
That's because—

00:17:41.810 --> 00:17:44.850
It was to save humanity, of course.

00:17:45.600 --> 00:17:46.690
You...

00:17:47.440 --> 00:17:48.940
Give Remy back to us!

00:17:49.270 --> 00:17:50.980
Remy is perfectly fine.

00:17:51.820 --> 00:17:54.200
We do not kill humans.

00:17:54.400 --> 00:17:58.320
We render them powerless
and store their psyches as data.

00:17:58.530 --> 00:18:01.080
Despite everything,
we are a humane weapon.

00:18:01.950 --> 00:18:06.170
We ended this war
without killing anybody.

00:18:06.460 --> 00:18:08.500
If we were not here,

00:18:08.500 --> 00:18:12.130
the two worlds would probably
have destroyed one another.

00:18:12.880 --> 00:18:17.840
Humans instinctively fight,
and we give them salvation.

00:18:18.050 --> 00:18:22.270
Within us, humanity can find eternal peace.

00:18:22.270 --> 00:18:24.600
Just like how I was earlier?

00:18:24.930 --> 00:18:29.900
All of humanity can experience
an eternal, blissful dream.

00:18:30.690 --> 00:18:34.990
That... you call that salvation?

00:18:35.360 --> 00:18:41.450
There is no need to worry.
Because... everything has already ended.

00:18:41.790 --> 00:18:42.910
Disappear!

00:18:47.250 --> 00:18:48.250
Are you all right?

00:18:49.630 --> 00:18:50.590
Yes.

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:53.050
But, my power is about to run out...

00:18:53.630 --> 00:18:57.090
I want you to tell me...
what should we do?

00:18:58.430 --> 00:19:00.970
At your current technological level...

00:19:01.430 --> 00:19:03.970
If we have Energy Cubes, we can evolve.

00:19:06.180 --> 00:19:09.520
But if we do that,
we're playing right into their hands.

00:19:09.520 --> 00:19:13.360
I had wanted to warn you
before the fighting began.

00:19:13.610 --> 00:19:21.240
But the Timekeepers were interfering,
and my voice did not reach you.

00:19:21.780 --> 00:19:24.040
But the fighting has already started.

00:19:24.290 --> 00:19:27.000
Perhaps I got here too late.

00:19:31.380 --> 00:19:33.800
The Energy Cube links us to the future.

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:37.590
You told me...
that the future was not determined yet.

00:19:38.840 --> 00:19:40.930
Normally, that would be correct.

00:19:41.260 --> 00:19:47.430
However, the Energy Cubes that the Timekeepers
 give you are linked to their future.

00:19:49.640 --> 00:19:51.600
We can't disconnect that link?

00:19:52.230 --> 00:19:56.230
We can... with my power,
it can... be undone.

00:19:56.860 --> 00:19:59.950
If you wish to create a future you desire...

00:19:59.950 --> 00:20:00.780
Then...

00:20:00.780 --> 00:20:04.740
However, the birth of Dead End
is an inevitable course of history...

00:20:04.950 --> 00:20:07.910
A few irregulars... the result... same...

00:20:08.710 --> 00:20:10.330
We can change it drastically!

00:20:10.330 --> 00:20:16.460
You are one of the eligible...
with that power... but if you fail...

00:20:16.630 --> 00:20:19.170
You will, right now, be taken by Dead End...

00:20:19.720 --> 00:20:20.720
I don't care.

00:20:21.260 --> 00:20:23.180
That's better than
ending right here, right now.

00:20:23.430 --> 00:20:24.600
Hold on a minute.

00:20:25.890 --> 00:20:27.140
Let go of me!

00:20:27.140 --> 00:20:29.730
Don't force your future on us anymore!

00:20:31.520 --> 00:20:34.360
How do you know that
what she says is correct?

00:20:34.650 --> 00:20:38.360
I understand if you don't believe me...

00:20:38.360 --> 00:20:38.990
What?

00:20:39.530 --> 00:20:44.490
But perhaps she's forcing the future
she wishes on you as well?

00:20:45.030 --> 00:20:49.000
To believe in someone
can be a dangerous thing.

00:20:49.000 --> 00:20:50.120
That doesn't mean...

00:20:51.040 --> 00:20:54.670
...that cooping myself up in a dream,
and forsaking everyone else is a good thing!

00:20:54.670 --> 00:20:56.040
That just can't be!

00:20:56.710 --> 00:21:01.630
This girl fought for me... for us...
and shed her blood.

00:21:02.470 --> 00:21:06.640
That's why I want to believe in you.
No, I will believe in you.

00:21:29.450 --> 00:21:32.160
Wait. Don't disappear.

00:21:32.660 --> 00:21:35.330
I'm sure... we will meet again...

00:21:36.380 --> 00:21:39.050
in your future...

00:23:25.490 --> 00:23:27.240
Oh, my friend!

00:23:27.240 --> 00:23:28.910
Friendship is something easily broken.

00:23:28.910 --> 00:23:30.990
That's not true! Look at that!

00:23:30.990 --> 00:23:31.990
Something has appeared!

00:23:30.990 --> 00:23:37.290
<b>DEMON</b>

00:23:31.990 --> 00:23:35.700
Uniting before danger,
that's the power of friendship!

00:23:35.700 --> 00:23:37.290
My friend is using me as a shield!

00:23:37.290 --> 00:23:38.360
Next episode: "Battlefield."

00:23:37.290 --> 00:23:40.000
<b><i>BATTLEFIELD </i></b>THE PRICE OF BLOODSHED

00:23:38.360 --> 00:23:40.000
"The Price of Bloodshed."
